================================================================================
Why AGPL-3.0?
================================================================================
SI-1 is designed to run as a system service (`/opt/si1`) on a sovereign OS
distribution (antiX base) with `llama-server` instances launched at init
level under `chmod 700` enforcement. This is a *network-facing deployment*
of constitutional AI governance.

AGPL-3.0 §13 ("Remote Network Interaction; Use with the GNU General Public
License") was chosen deliberately so that:
  (a) Anyone embedding SI-1 in a hosted product, container image, ISO, or
      VM snapshot must publish their modifications to the source.
  (b) The constitutional prompts (`core/system.md`, `core/observer_system.md`)
      and runtime cannot be quietly replaced by a downstream fork and
      redistributed as SI-1 without disclosure.
  (c) The "honorable collaboration" posture is enforced as a license
      obligation, not merely a request.

This is recorded as ADR-0004 in `docs/decisions.md`.
